    "status": "present",
    "value": "Model each (n-1)-digit string as a node. Appending digit d to node u gives an n-digit password and moves to the node made of the last n-1 digits. Each password is exactly one edge, every node has k outgoing and k incoming edges, so an Eulerian circuit exists and visits every edge once. Writing the starting node (n-1 zeros) followed by the edge digits in circuit order gives a string of length k^n + n - 1 containing every password. The candidate runs Hierholzer's algorithm with an explicit stack, using a per-node counter of used outgoing edges, and emits digits when edges are popped."
  },
